  "description": "catalog rebuild makes a new catalog from what the disks hold, every copy read whole, and sets the old one aside, never removing it; without --yes it says so and exits with 3, and with --dry-run with 0. Copies with different hashes at one path are a conflict, whatever else they share. The new catalog's operations start past the highest id the disks' trash and tmp/ name, and what those folders hold is left as it is; the entry of t2's trash is listed again.",
